\begin{abstract}
Tape diagrams provide a graphical representation for arrows of rig categories, namely categories equipped with two monoidal structures, $\piu$ and $\per$, where $\per$ distributes over $\piu$. However, their applicability is limited to categories where $\piu$ is a biproduct, i.e., both a categorical product and a coproduct. In this work, we 
extend tape diagrams to deal with Kleisli categories of symmetric monoidal monads, presented by algebraic theories.
\end{abstract}

