\section{Conclusion}
We present a practical and minimax-optimal algorithm for batched linear bandits that unifies theoretical tightness and empirical efficiency. By integrating arm elimination with a regularized G-optimal design, Our method achieves $\widetilde{\Ocal}\bigl(\sqrt{dT\log K} \,\wedge\, d\sqrt{T}\bigr)$ regret in only $\Ocal(\log\log T)$ batches, matching known lower bounds for both large-$K$ and small-$K$ regimes. 
