\subsubsection{\textbf{Theoretical analysis}} \label{sec:6.3.3}
In this experiment, we discuss whether our proposed incentive mechanism is bounded by Propositions \ref{prop:1} and \ref{prop:2} and present the results in Fig. \ref{fig9}. Notably, the theoretical upper bound of $\gamma$ and $\epsilon$ primarily stem from (\ref{eq:50}), so we will assess the effectiveness of our proposed incentive mechanism via the probability gap $\gamma_{i^*}\epsilon_{i^*} - \gamma\epsilon$. Here, we consider that the theoretical upper bound $\gamma_{i^*}\epsilon_{i^*}$ is calculated as per the first inequality of (\ref{eq:50}), i.e., $\gamma_{i^*} \epsilon_{i^*} \rho (\beta - 1) = W$.

