\leq m \hspace{-0.07cm}\ \text{exp}(-\lambda_0 s) \ \text{for all} \  s\geq 0,    \nonumber \end{eqnarray}
\item[\textit{iii)}] If $-F(\mathcal{G}(t))$ is differentiable and there exist scalars $\alpha>0$ and $0<\mu<\frac{\beta_1}{2\beta_2^3}$ such that for all $t$, $T\geq 0$,
