    g^*_D := g_D(-0.75553,..., -0.75553) \approx -1.3911
\end{equation}
By contrast with Family \#1, Family \#2 is asymmetric about the origin. Further, the cost of evaluating the objective in this case is significantly higher; the functions $g_D(\cdot)$ each have $N_{g_D} = O(D^3)$ non-zero coefficients compared with $O(D)$ for Family \#1. This results in more costly computations as discussed below. Once again, experiments were performed using the Algorithm described in Section \ref{sec:algorithm} with parameters detailed in Table \ref{tab:param_family_2}. Given such higher cost, we considered dimensions from $1$ to $45$ only. As before, a relative error of $10^{-2}$ is expected using such parameters.

