\section{Conclusion}

While users typically have a long-term preference profile built up over a long period of time, there are short-term effects that may affect preferences as well.  In this work, we establish that different types of `experts' that focus on either short- or long-term preference would work better together, as not only do both types of preferences matter, but the way they do so differs from user to user.  Which model predominates also varies across datasets, emphasizing the proposed framework approach of \proposedcove, leveraging on multiple experts working in concert, while accommodating a gating mechanism that modulates the influence of each expert on recommendations.

