\section{Dataset: Fibonacci Small Blocks (FiboSB)}
\jf{To demonstrate the potential of using 6D pose estimation for collaborative group work in an educational setting, we introduce the FiboSB dataset. FiboSB is based on the Weights Task Dataset (WTD) \cite{khebour2024text}, which involves a group of triads \sm{interacting with} six colored blocks \cj{  (two $1.5$ $inch^{3}$ and four $2.0$ $inch^{3}$)} and a weight scale to determine the weights of each block. The group is initially given the weight of one block, and then they are tasked with finding the weights of the rest of the colored blocks, which follows a Fibonacci sequence. In FiboSB, we annotate the 6D poses of the colored blocks in the WTD so that we can train and evaluate 6D pose estimation models.}

%We introduce a 6D pose estimation in an educational setting, especially collaborative group work. For recording teamwork, a Fibonacci weight task is provided to each group, and six colored blocks are used as the main objects to achieve the goal of the task. Every single record is composed of three participants who have never experienced the task, and we ask them to guess the order of weights of the blocks. Since the dataset covers the Fibonacci weight task using small blocks, we call it as Fibonacci Small Blocks(FiboSB), and the dataset contains 10 recorded videos and corresponding annotations. More details about data collection and annotation procedure are described in Sec \ref{sec:data_collection} and \ref{sec:annotation_procedure} respectively.

